<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch BNG says profits rise five percent in 1996.</title>
<headline>Dutch BNG says profits rise five percent in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>De Bank Nederlandse Gemeenten (BNG) said on Thursday that profits rose five percent to 316 million guilders in 1996.</p>
<p>BNG's shareholders, the Dutch state, the provinces and towns, will receive a total dividend of 133 million guilders, eight million more than a year earlier.</p>
<p>The local authorities bank, a major borrower on the international capital markets, also said the 225 million guilder balance of its VAR, or provision for general contingencies, would be transferred to the new FAR, or fund for general risks.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +020 - 504 5000</p>
